Structure follows Tunisia where it genuinely applies (Net Pay, Employer Contribution, Banking Details, Footer Details) and adds the four Belgium-only blocks Tunisia has no analogue for. Content is grounded, not copied: every `$…custom.*` token in a new row matches a real **BE-DD-001** field name (`NSSO Worker Code`, `Mean Weekly Working Hours`, `Holiday Entitlement in Days`, `Wage Payment Method`, `Employee Bank Account IBAN`, `Language Regime of Personnel Documents`, …) and every code cited resolves to a populated Mercans Code in **BE-WTC-001** (23671, BE-012, 62160, 62901, 62660, 62870, BE-006).

Format matches the existing sheet exactly — navy `FF1F3864` banners with white bold Calibri 10, teal `FF4BACC6` / orange `FFF79646` column headers, `FFF2F2F2` alternate banding, thin `FFBFBFBF` borders, same 4-column layout and column widths. **The 37 pre-existing rows were read out of the workbook and re-emitted programmatically rather than retyped — verified 37/37 preserved verbatim.**

## Fix 2 — BE-PSL-002: stated rule corrected

`Belgium (EN)!B82` + `!A112` and `Belgium (NL)!B82` + `!A112`. `A112` now carries the full six-band table from BE-CCG-001 Table 40 and states that the band is selected on the wage of the quarter actually paid — so a quarter carrying double holiday pay or the end-of-year premium falls in a higher band, which is why the quarterly amounts in the YTD block differ. `B82` names which band this specimen's quarter falls in. **No formula and no figure changed** (asserted in the script; `I82`, `I92` and all 55 formula cells untouched).

## Fix 3 — BE-PSL-004: language gap completed

`Belgium (EN)!A109` and `Belgium (NL)!A109` now name all three regions: Dutch delivered, French a mandatory second deliverable, German an explicit unbuilt seam — matching `scope_manifest.json!known_limitations` on which is which. Side effect: this removed the word "pending", so the widened marker sweep now returns **0 hits on all six BE-authored sheets** (was 1).

